It&#x2019;s difficult to imagine a song choice more precisely capturing the essence of a movie than Boz Scaggs&#x2019; mellow yacht rock groove &#x201C;Lowdown,&#x201D; which kicks off the end credits of The Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth . That might seem odd for a gritty comedy that builds to an ultraviolent climactic bloodbath, but this standalone chapter in the life of the now-retired stuntman from Once Upon a Time in Hollywood &#x2014; the role that won Brad Pitt an Oscar &#x2014; saunters along to its own idiosyncratic beat, running on a well-lubricated R&B engine. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The star&#x2019;s golden glow and loose-limbed charisma, David Fincher &#x2019;s exactingly controlled direction and the shaggier storytelling style of Quentin Tarantino &#x2019;s screenplay are not always the most seamless fit. But the obvious mutual esteem and affection shared by that creative triumvirate is contagious and the movie has a good-time vibe that just won&#x2019;t quit &#x2014; even if it feels more stretched and less substantive than its 2019 predecessor. Still, few fans will complain, especially those who opt for the IMAX experience, before it hits Netflix on Dec. 23. Related Stories Movies Ron Howard Wasn't Sure He Was the Right Director for 'Avedon'; This Is What Changed His Mind TV Netflix to Adapt 'Grendel' Comic Books Into Adult Animated TV Series The Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth The Bottom Line Sexy, seductive and chaotic in mostly fun ways. Release date : Weds., Nov. 25 (in theaters); Weds., Dec. 23 (streaming) Cast : Brad Pitt, Elizabeth Debicki, Scott Caan, Carla Gugino, Yahya Abdul-Mateen II, Peter Weller, Matt Groove, JB Tadena, Corey Fogelmanis, Karren Karagulian, Lauren Glazier, Timothy Olyphant, Nicholas Hammond Director : David Fincher Screenwriter : Quentin Tarantino Rated R, 2 hours 23 minutes

Eight years have passed since Cliff and Leonardo DiCaprio&#x2019;s faded TV star Rick Dalton, for whom Pitt&#x2019;s character worked as a longtime stunt double, mopped up three homicidal Manson followers &#x2014; described here as &#x201C;those fuckin&#x2019; hippie intruders&#x201D; &#x2014; in pools of their own blood. Rick is now starring in a TV series in Australia drolly titled Dingo Dan , and Cliff has aged out of the stunt game, though his is not an idle retirement.

He works as a projectionist at the New Beverly Cinema &#x2014; the historic repertory house in the Fairfax district now owned and programmed by Tarantino as a 35mm stronghold &#x2014; where the fictional blaxploitation film Soul Brothers Die Hard has been such a hit that Cliff can recite the dialogue along with the actors. Its cast is topped by former Oakland Raiders player Roderick &#x201C;Hot Rod&#x201D; Harrison ( Yahya Abdul-Mateen II ), who opens Fincher&#x2019;s film with a quintessential Tarantino provocation, enlightening his character&#x2019;s nephew about &#x201C;how to keep multiple bitches turnt out.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Cliff also mixes killer cocktails at a rowdy Redondo Beach tiki bar that features female mud-wrestling contests and picks up occasional work as &#x201C;a day player&#x201D; on XXX porn movies, including one currently in production titled The Sexorcist . For recreation, he participates in punishing demolition derby meets.

But Cliff&#x2019;s main source of off-the-books income is as a fixer operating outside the law to solve problems for rich Angelenos in a jam. One task he&#x2019;s assigned is to retrieve jewelry and a best director Oscar stolen from a married Hollywood veteran by Joey (Corey Fogelmanis), the young hustler he picked up outside Astro Burger on Santa Monica Blvd. When Joey shows up at the New Beverly with criminal associate Chicken Hawk (Sean Baker favorite Karren Karagulian) to exchange the goods for a wad of cash, Cliff turns the transaction to his advantage with brisk decisiveness and zero conscience.

Pitt&#x2019;s Cliff in Once Upon a Time was very much a sidekick, a laid-back man of few words compared to Rick. This time around, he&#x2019;s become a much more loquacious operator. But the film&#x2019;s episodic nature &#x2014; jumping around in time and neighborhood, shifts marked in onscreen text &#x2014; makes the early action ambling and discursive. It takes an inordinate amount of time to settle on a central plot thread. Is it a romance? A crime thriller? A dark comedy? A hangout movie whose foremost concern is nostalgic time travel to late &#x2018;70s Los Angeles? Actually, it&#x2019;s all those things, though it can feel unfocused. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The narrative wheels kick into gear when Cliff gets a call from talent agent Karen Crosby ( Elizabeth Debicki , never better), whose TV star client Charlie Peters ( Scott Caan ) has requested a meeting. Given that Charlie is known for doing all his own stunts &#x2014; a detour into his career highlights shows B&W footage from popular series with titles like Fireball Jungle , Tom Horn: Stock Detective and Enemy Territory , along with an appearance on the Johnny Carson show &#x2014; Cliff is perplexed as to the purpose of the meeting and Karen is unforthcoming with details. It&#x2019;s likely she hasn&#x2019;t even been let in on what Charlie wants.

Meanwhile, a pair of gangster brothers in town from the Philippines for a job, Eddie (Matt Groove) and Fernando Verdusco (JB Tadena), start making their presence felt, first with a jolt of horrific violence when they break into a family&#x2019;s home in an upscale neighborhood. Even by Tarantino&#x2019;s standards the brutal ugliness of that incident is shocking, made even more vicious by Eddie&#x2019;s weapon of choice, a massive hammer he calls Esmarelda.

It turns out Charlie partied hard with the Verduscos while shooting in the Philippines, coincidentally where Cliff served in World War II, while the country was under Japanese occupation. On a drunken impulse, Charlie hired the brothers to eliminate a problem and although he has tried to back out of the deal, they have come to follow through and collect. That puts the TV star, Cliff and even Hot Rod in danger, since he and Charlie are shooting a private eye TV movie called Disco Kingpin . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

There&#x2019;s an Elmore Leonard kinship in the crime elements; Fincher takes his cue from Tarantino by making us squirm and laugh through even the most sadistic acts. But the movie lavishes just as much time and attention on Cliff&#x2019;s slow-burn romancing of Karen and his playful banter with Charlie&#x2019;s wife Toni ( Carla Gugino ), with whom he had a fling &#x2014; unbeknownst to Charlie &#x2014; while they were working on a Rick Dalton dud titled Salty the Talking Sea Otter . A tennis club doubles match with Cliff and Karen playing Charlie and Toni is key to establishing the latter&#x2019;s significance in a tricky scenario to be revealed.

It&#x2019;s no surprise that Cliff takes charge of Charlie&#x2019;s predicament, never losing his cool even when he&#x2019;s seriously at risk. As much as the movie is enamored with L.A., its period landmarks and the usual load of pop-culture ephemera so beloved by Tarantino, it&#x2019;s also a big fat valentine to guys like Cliff, chill dudes cut from the same cloth as Steve McQueen. The film is more driven by casual vignettes than complex action set pieces, even if the spectacularly bloody final act is up there with Tarantino&#x2019;s most operatic explosions of violence.

Often, The Further Mis-Adventures is so busy swooning over Brad/Cliff that it plays like episodic TV or part of a pulpy paperback series built around the lovable reprobate character. It&#x2019;s less robust as a feature-length narrative, though that doesn&#x2019;t make it any less entertaining. Tarantino disciples will eat it up, while Fincher obsessives should find plenty of the director&#x2019;s pungent atmospherics, his technical flair and moody visual style. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid4' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Cliff&#x2019;s inevitable showdown with the Verduscos seems not so much a story in its own right as a chapter in the man&#x2019;s personal mythology to go along with the legends that Charlie recaps with breathless hero worship &#x2014; notably that time he took down Bruce Lee. Tarantino doubles down on that here, thumbing his nose at the many people who found his irreverent besmirching of the martial arts icon insulting.

Caan is doing some of his best work, amusingly bouncing Charlie&#x2019;s excitability off Cliff&#x2019;s relaxed stoner gestalt or Karen&#x2019;s self-possessed composure. For once using her native accent and taking full advantage of her imposing height, Debicki is in sublime command of her powers playing a savvy, languidly sensual Australian gal who is nobody&#x2019;s idea of a delicate flower. Her chemistry with Pitt is off the charts.

At one point Crosby, as Cliff calls her, is seen attending the splashy premiere of Looking for Mr. Goodbar , photographed like a goddess in a fabulously draped white halter pantsuit and scarf &#x2014; an unwise choice later that evening when she goes to a mud-caked figure-eight track and is surprised to find Cliff among the drivers. Even in moments that might be considered humiliating for many screen glamazons, Karen&#x2019;s authority never falters. And she is equally adept at delivering a left and right hook.

Gugino also brings her A-game to a smart character who accepts her husband for the overgrown boy he is but by no means is immune to the flirty sexual frisson of a more mature hunk. The actress also looks nothing short of sensational. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid5' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

There&#x2019;s not a weak link in the ensemble. Abdul-Mateen is very clearly having a blast playing outrageous stereotypes in the fictional film and TV scenes within the movie, and when Rod is not on a screen or in front of a camera he carries himself with the effortless swagger of a former pro-footballer turned badass movie star.

The other vital cast contribution comes from Peter Weller as Cliff&#x2019;s dad Gus, who, when not behind the counter at his pawn shop &#x2014; where he teaches junkies how capitalism works &#x2014; consumes an unending diet of TV, whether it&#x2019;s The Rockford Files , Bonanza or Hee Haw . Father and son share an apartment in a sprawling Marina del Rey complex, where their spiky exchanges never obscure the nourishing love they get from each other. Mostly, Gus just wants Cliff to feed his cat and stop blocking the TV.

While the &#x2018;70s New Hollywood reference is clear, Fincher and cinematographer Erik Messerschmidt &#x2014; shooting on digital, a departure from Tarantino's devotion to celluloid &#x2014; perhaps lean into the dark, grubby look a little too eagerly, though the noirish aspect fits, echoed in Trent Reznor and Atticus Ross&#x2019; supple score.

Courtesy of Ren Klyce's densely layered sound design, those orchestral interludes are woven in with a dizzying array of needle drops that make you wonder how much Netflix spent on music rights. (The unexpected use of Electric Light Orchestra&#x2019;s peppy &#x201C;Tightrope&#x201D; over one violent sequence is inspired, and there's not one but two Donna Summer tracks that absolutely slap.) Production and costume design from Don Burt and Trish Summerville, respectively, are a riot of period nods that never drift into kitsch. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid6' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Ultimately, however, the key ingredient binding together a movie that seldom meets an abrupt tangent it declines to explore is Pitt. His star wattage, shit-eating grin and cowboy gait &#x2014; even with a limp and a body full of bones on which decades of stunt work have taken their toll &#x2014; are dialed up to maximum magnetism.

America's favorite quiz show is welcoming fans to Washington, D.C., for a three-day event celebrating all things "Jeopardy!" Taking place May 7 to 9, 2027, the convention will feature live programming, engaging panels, interactive quizzes and exclusive merchandise.

Jeopardy!Con will feature behind-the-scenes sessions with iconic players from the trivia show, plus exclusive announcements and contestant casting opportunities. The weekend will also include a welcome party, closing celebration and other social gatherings. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Queen Latifah, Bone Thugs-N-Harmony, MC Lyte and More to Lead 2027 Rock the Bells Cruise

Perhaps the most exciting aspect of Jeopardy!Con is an all-new live "Jeopardy!" competition format featuring famous players competing in front of thousands of fans. "The two-night marquee event will bring the game to life on a scale never before seen at 'Jeopardy!,'" according to a press release.

Tickets will go on sale in early 2027, with additional programming to be announced.

&#x201C;People are looking for meaningful ways to connect, and few things bring people together quite like a shared passion,&#x201D; said Suzanne Prete, president of game shows at Sony Pictures Television. &#x201C;For generations, 'Jeopardy!' has united fans through a love of knowledge, curiosity and competition. Jeopardy!Con builds on that legacy in an entirely new way, creating an unprecedented opportunity to bring fans together to celebrate the show, connect with one another and experience the franchise like never before.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Ever since I joined 'Jeopardy!' in 2021, I&#x2019;ve wanted to bring this extraordinary community together in a way that&#x2019;s bigger than anything we&#x2019;ve done before and give fans the chance to interact with their quiz show heroes,&#x201D; said Michael Davies, executive producer of "Jeopardy!" &#x201C;One of the remarkable things we&#x2019;ve seen through our live podcast and 'Jeopardy!' interactive events all over the country is just how much people want to come together and share their love of the game. Everyone on the team is incredibly excited to bring it all together next May.&#x201D;

Javier Calvo was traveling with his filmmaking partner, Javier Ambrossi, when he read Alberto Conejero&#x2019;s play La Piedra Oscura ( The Dark Stone ) and the idea for La Bola Negra ( The Black Ball ) took hold. Conejero&#x2019;s drama, set in a military hospital during the Spanish Civil War, imagines the last night of Rafael Rodr&#xED;guez Rap&#xFA;n &#x2014; a Republican lieutenant and the real-life lover of playwright Federico Garc&#xED;a Lorca &#x2014; in conversation with Sebasti&#xE1;n, the young Nationalist soldier who is to execute him at dawn.

&#x201C;I imagined this little gay boy having to leave his town, all this tragedy, and how this happened to my country only 90 years ago, and having a gay character in the civil war,&#x201D; says Calvo. &#x201C;We never talk about that. Where were we? What happened to us? It hit me, and I started to cry. I told Javi, &#x2018;I think we have to make this.&#x2019; &#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies 'Obsession' Breakout Inde Navarrette to Receive Spotlight Tribute at Gotham Film Awards (Exclusive) Movies The Free World Award Is Made From Weapons Metal. The First Winner: Iraq's Oscar Entry

The film, co-written with Conejero, braids three timelines. In 1932 Granada, Carlos (Milo Quifes), a young upper-class Andalusian, is blackballed from an exclusive casino because he&#x2019;s gay &#x2014; the premise of Lorca&#x2019;s unfinished play La Bola Negra , of which only four pages survive. In 1937, Sebasti&#xE1;n (singer- songwriter Guitarricadelafuente ) keeps watch over Rafael (Miguel Bernardeau). And in 2017 Madrid, Alberto (Carlos Gonz&#xE1;lez) learns that he is Sebasti&#xE1;n&#x2019;s grandson. Sebasti&#xE1;n has left him the rest of Lorca&#x2019;s play &#x2014; pages the film imagines into being &#x2014; which he had promised Rafael he would save. Those pages &#x2014; verified by Glenn Close, who plays a Spanish-speaking American scholar named Isabelle Durand &#x2014; lead Alberto and his relatives to discover that Sebasti&#xE1;n spent most of his life secretly living with another man. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;This is a movie about what we pass on to the next generation,&#x201D; Ambrossi says. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s about inheritance.&#x201D;

The co-directors, known as Los Javis among their collaborators because of their shared first names, reassembled their usual crafts team to begin shaping each timeline: cinematographer Gris Jordana, editor Alberto Guti&#xE9;rrez, production designer Roger Bell&#xE9;s, costume designer Ana L&#xF3;pez Cobos, composer Ra&#xFC;l Refree and casting directors Eva Leira and Yolanda Serrano.

The directors were already keen on Guitarricadelafuente and Bernardeau for their respective roles, as well as Gonz&#xE1;lez for the part of Alberto, which Ambrossi calls &#x201C;a creation.&#x201D;

&#x201C;He&#x2019;s so comedic and flamboyant, but we wanted to give him a role where he can prove the actor that he is because sometimes queer people are given the same [stereotypical] roles,&#x201D; Ambrossi says.

Quifes, who like Guitarricadelafuente makes his screen debut in the film, was found through an open casting call. &#x201C;He has a sense of melancholy about him, but it&#x2019;s not about hopelessness; there&#x2019;s a sense of hope and beauty,&#x201D; says Leira. &#x201C;And he has such a beautiful gaze. It&#x2019;s a gaze that comes from ancient times.&#x201D;

Los Javis also knew they wanted to shoot in 35mm from the outset, which aligned with DP Jordana&#x2019;s approach. &#x201C;You don&#x2019;t have to fight the format to get images,&#x201D; she says of 35mm film. &#x201C;If you use the right light direction, the rest just comes together. It&#x2019;s like magic.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Light also drove the design of the opulent casino in Granada, the only set built from scratch. Everywhere else, the production restored existing buildings, hiring local artisans who still work with prewar methods. &#x201C;At first glance, it looked like something crazy and unnecessary when we built it in the middle of Spain, but when you open the windows, you see Spain, not a green screen,&#x201D; says production designer Bell&#xE9;s, who commissioned artist Ignasi Monreal to paint the mural on the ceiling in the style of Joaqu&#xED;n Sorolla, &#x201C;one of the great painters of Spanish light,&#x201D; he explains.

The windows were made of sugar glass so that they could shatter safely when the casino explodes near the end of the film after being overtaken by a mob as Carlos makes a final case for admission. The remaining structure was then filled with fake snow as the scene transitions to Carlos lying on a mountainside, realizing he has died from the bomb&#x2019;s explosion. The shot, captured at an altitude of 3,000 meters (more than 9,800 feet high) in the snowy region of the Sierra Nevadas, brought to life elements described in Lorca&#x2019;s poem &#x2014; like the skiers on the slopes &#x2014; which also inspired Guitarricadelafuente&#x2019;s original song, &#x201C;La Nieve (The Snow),&#x201D; that plays in the background.

&#x201C;With Federico Garc&#xED;a Lorca, there&#x2019;s a lot of powerful imagery and symbolism, like in the beginning of the film, the horse running past Sebasti&#xE1;n is a representation of untamable desire,&#x201D; Guitarricadelafuente explains. &#x201C; &#x2018;La Nieve&#x2019; symbolized the end of a journey and approaching death. I had to leave the emotional baggage of Sebasti&#xE1;n to fully understand what he was carrying to be able to write that.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Refree took a hands-on approach with Pen&#xE9;lope Cruz, who portrays Nen&#xE9; Romero, a cupletista cabaret singer. &#x201C;She told me, &#x2018;I&#x2019;m not a singer,&#x2019; but as soon as I heard her singing &#x2026; I fell in love with her singing,&#x201D; he says. &#x201C;The problem was that she hadn&#x2019;t created the character yet.&#x201D;

Over the course of several days, Refree went to Cruz&#x2019;s home for rehearsals, and she began to craft the persona of Nen&#xE9;, who serves as a portal to a world in which Sebasti&#xE1;n can be free to be his true self when he sees her perform &#x201C;Las Tardes del Ritz (Afternoons at the Ritz)&#x201D; and &#x201C;Batall&#xF3;n de modistillas (Seamstress Battalion)&#x201D; on the base.

&#x201C;My goal was to have this kind of music that she could be influenced by when talking to the soldiers and to create this evocative thing, like making two men play together as a couple,&#x201D; Refree explains of the first number. &#x201C;The second one needed a dirty energy that would make the soldiers lose control and want to touch her. So we created something very rhythmic and feminine at the same time.&#x201D;

Wardrobe also helped shape Nen&#xE9;. Cobos drew from research on 19th century cupl&#xE9; singers, like Mar&#xED;a del Consuelo Vello Cano, to sketch Cruz&#x2019;s feathery, embellished ensemble.

&#x201C;When she saw the white dress, she said, &#x2018;This is it; she has to be wearing white,&#x2019; and Gris also said it would be helpful because we don&#x2019;t have a lot of lights in the theater,&#x201D; says Cobos. &#x201C;[For the second number,] because I know Pen&#xE9;lope&#x2019;s a big fan of Mugler, I went through their images and found these overalls and dresses that reminded me of military costumes. So I did my own interpretation of them, and it worked really well because it helped her move and it was very comfortable for her to do the choreography with the tank and all of the other dancers.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid4' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

In the final scene of the film, Sebasti&#xE1;n reads a poem with the words, &#x201C; Mira, que nos acechan todavia (Beware, they still haunt us),&#x201D; after being forced to shoot Rafael. It&#x2019;s the final verse of &#x201C;Love Sleeps in the Poet&#x2019;s Breast,&#x201D; one of the Sonetos del Amor Oscuro ( Sonnets of Dark Love ), written by Lorca for Rafael, expressing his forbidden desire for him amid the looming threat of societal persecution.

For Calvo, the warning is just as relevant today. &#x201C;We had it on the whiteboard, and it was kind of a guide [for us],&#x201D; he says. &#x201C;Putting it [at the end of the film] was perfect and so significant because they do still haunt us.&#x201D;

This story appeared in the Nov. 18 issue of The Hollywood Reporter magazine. Click here to subscribe .

EXCLUSIVE: Hello Uglies! The Boulet Brothers are back for another round of glam nightmare fuel at Shudder , which has given the drag duo's reality competition franchise a renewal.

